[N1a] --- nu-uniformity of BFG Thm 8/10 ---
[N1b] NS_nu[nu*v(x,nu t)] - nu^2 * NS_1[v](x,nu t) = Matrix([[0, 0, 0]])  (zero vector => exact)
[N1c] T*||omega_0||_inf at viscosity nu = 1/c  (nu cancels exactly => the clock is nu-uniform)
[N2a] --- heat-kernel moments in R^3, G(z,tau)=(4 pi tau)^{-3/2} exp(-|z|^2/4tau) ---
[N2b] tau=1         int G dz = 1.000000000000   int |grad G| dz = 1.12837917   vs 2/sqrt(pi tau) = 1.12837917
[N2b] tau=0.01      int G dz = 1.000000000000   int |grad G| dz = 11.28379167   vs 2/sqrt(pi tau) = 11.28379167
[N2b] tau=0.0001    int G dz = 1.000000000000   int |grad G| dz = 112.83791671   vs 2/sqrt(pi tau) = 112.83791671
[N2c] MC mean of grad G / G = -z/(2tau) under G(.,1):  [-5.36813311e-04  1.19239104e-05  7.12757985e-04]  (-> 0 : int grad G dz = 0 exactly, by oddness)
[N2d] consequence: adding a constant C to the integrand changes int G*(.) by C but int grad G*(.) by 0.  The velocity/divergence-form mild equation may therefore subtract the local average for free; BFG's (8) third term (kernel = G, integrand |omega||grad u| >= 0) may not.
[N3a] --- vorticity clock implied by GIM Remark (i) [velocity] via Biot-Savart ---
[N3b] optimal rho = 2**(1/3)*W2**(2/3)/(2*M**(2/3)) ;  ||u_0||_inf <~ 3*2**(1/3)*M**(1/3)*W2**(2/3)/2
[N3c] GIM T >= C/||u_0||_inf^2  =>  M*T >~ 2*2**(1/3)*M**(1/3)/(9*W2**(4/3))
[N3d] M*T >~ Re_om^(-1/3) with Re_om = ||om_0||_2^4/||om_0||_inf ; check M*T * Re_om**Rational(1,3) = 2*2**(1/3)/9
[N3e] scaling of Re_om under om->lam^2 om(lam x): 1  (=1 => dimensionless)
[N4a] --- own compactly supported family h_R = (1 - log(1+|x|)/log R)_+ ---
[N4b] R=1e2   int h_R/(1+|x|)^4 = 2.548370   1/log R = 2.171e-01   ratio I*log R (grows linearly) =     11.74   I/(4pi/3) = 0.6084
[N4b] R=1e4   int h_R/(1+|x|)^4 = 3.355141   1/log R = 1.086e-01   ratio I*log R (grows linearly) =     30.90   I/(4pi/3) = 0.8010
[N4b] R=1e8   int h_R/(1+|x|)^4 = 3.771897   1/log R = 5.429e-02   ratio I*log R (grows linearly) =     69.48   I/(4pi/3) = 0.9005
[N4b] R=1e16  int h_R/(1+|x|)^4 = 3.980344   1/log R = 2.714e-02   ratio I*log R (grows linearly) =    146.64   I/(4pi/3) = 0.9502
[N4b] R=1e32  int h_R/(1+|x|)^4 = 4.084567   1/log R = 1.357e-02   ratio I*log R (grows linearly) =    300.96   I/(4pi/3) = 0.9751
[N4b] R=1e64  int h_R/(1+|x|)^4 = 4.136679   1/log R = 6.786e-03   ratio I*log R (grows linearly) =    609.60   I/(4pi/3) = 0.9876
[N4c] 4*pi/3 = 4.188790 ; the left side tends to 4pi/3 while ||h_R||_BMO -> 0 like 1/log R, so no absolute constant c can exist.  (Third independent family; agrees with the two refuter seats.)
[N5a] --- BFG's iteration with the local-average term restored ---
[N5b] invariance of the ball {||om||<=2 c0 M} holds iff t <= 1/(4*Lambda*M*c0*c1)
[N5c] Lambda = 1 (BFG as displayed) -> T ~ 1/(4 c0 c1 M): their Theorem 8. Lambda = 1 + log_+(ell/sqrt(nu/M)) (the restored local average) -> T ~ 1/(M (1+log Re)): a logarithmic clock.  The two statements differ ONLY by this factor.
[N6a] --- Euler-side tension: Kim-Jeong Prop 4.1 exponents ---
[N6b] T(m) = c_1*m**(alpha/2 - 1/2)*(1 - alpha); growth >= (1/4) m^(c_2-alpha); ||om_0||_(L1 cap Linf) <= eps
[N6c] alpha=0.1:  M_0*T(m) <= eps*['1.133e-01', '1.426e-02', '2.261e-04', '5.679e-08'] at m=1e2,1e4,1e8,1e16 -> 0
[N6c] alpha=0.2:  M_0*T(m) <= eps*['1.268e-01', '2.010e-02', '5.048e-04', '3.185e-07'] at m=1e2,1e4,1e8,1e16 -> 0
[N6c] alpha=0.24:  M_0*T(m) <= eps*['1.321e-01', '2.295e-02', '6.931e-04', '6.321e-07'] at m=1e2,1e4,1e8,1e16 -> 0
[N6d] so on the Euler side M_0 * (doubling time) -> 0 along that family, i.e. the Euler analogue of BFG Thm 10 is FALSE.  BFG Thm 10 is nu-uniform [N1c].  A rigorous inviscid limit on the Euler existence interval would therefore contradict it.  NOT ESTABLISHED here: the limit is not justified in this note.
